          "title": "You'll want to know: 大人",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "大人 — dàren — \"adult; grown-up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "大人和小孩都来了 dàren hé xiǎohái dōu lái le — The grown-ups and the children have all come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "大人 (dàren) is built from 大 'big' and 人 'a person', both inherited from Middle Chinese, daH and nyin (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). In the word the second loses its tone."
            }
          ]
        },
